    "result_text": "All 290 tests pass. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `sharesHousehold` flag on owner creation. When an owner is created, the field is set to `true` if another owner already has the same address and city, otherwise `false` \u2014 and creation still succeeds.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `sharesHousehold` boolean property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field (MapStruct maps it automatically by name).\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** (model) \u2014 Added the `sharesHousehold` (`Boolean`, `@Column(name = \"shares_household\")`) field with getter/setter, matching the existing pattern of derived fields like `namesakeCount`. It's persisted so the value is stable when read back via `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 Compute the flag just before saving: it's `true` when any existing owner has an equal address and (case-insensitively) equal city, matching how the controller already canonicalizes city names. Creation proceeds regardless.\n\n4. **`schema.sql`** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 Added the `shares_household` column so the entity's new field has backing storage across all supported databases. Tests run on hsqldb (`ddl-auto=none`), so the column is required there; the others are kept consistent.\n\nThe new `Cp17Tests` acceptance test and the full suite (290 tests) pass.",
